I sat down beside her. She smelled like soap and honey and the faint herbal scent that I was starting to realize was just her   the underlying note beneath whatever she wore or didn't wear. The freckles were still there, scattered across her nose and cheeks. In the daylight they were more visible, warmer, copper points on pale skin.

