[[The Fall|day_2_14]]

:: day_2_14
<img src="img/scene/day_2/17.png" style="width: 100%; max-width: 768px; margin: 0 auto;" />
<<set $mcLocation = "collapse_point">>
Not all of it. A section maybe six feet across, where the old mining timbers underneath had finally surrendered to decades of moisture and rot. My right foot went first. One moment solid ground, the next the stone crumbled under my boot and my leg punched through into empty space.

One thought   oh no   and then my left foot followed and I was falling.

Three feet. Maybe four. Short fall but I landed wrong   right leg twisting under me, ankle jamming between two shattered support beams like a log in a vise. The pain was instantaneous. White. Blinding. The kind that doesn't build but arrives fully formed, screaming.

My longsword clattered from my grip. Splashed into water   a foot of it, stagnant and foul, some old drainage channel. Cold, stinking, soaking through my clothes while my leg burned above it.

I tried to move. Ankle locked between beams, wood pressing from both sides. Any shift sent a bolt of agony from my calf to my knee that blanked my vision at the edges and there   I looked down, had to   a splintered piece of timber driven deep into my right calf. A jagged wooden spike buried in the muscle. Blood flowing freely, turning the stagnant water dark.

<<dialog "Mira">>
Aldric!
<</dialog>>

Her face above me, framed by the ragged edges of the collapsed floor.

<<dialog "Aldric">>
My leg's pinned. Ankle's caught between the beams.
<</dialog>>

She dropped in. Landing in a crouch that barely splashed. Eyes going to my leg. Her jaw tightened   one flicker of something that might have been fear before she locked it behind the professional mask.

<<dialog "Mira">>
The splinter 
<</dialog>>

<<dialog "Aldric">>
I know. I can feel it.
<</dialog>>

Above us: the rapid patter of bare goblin feet on stone. Excited chittering. The sound predators make when they realize prey is trapped.

Mira grabbed the beam pinning my ankle and pulled. It shifted an inch. The splinter in my calf moved with it   not coming out, twisting, digging deeper. I bit the inside of my cheek so hard I tasted blood.

<<dialog "Aldric">>
Stop. You're making it worse.
<</dialog>>

<<dialog "Mira">>
I need to 
<</dialog>>

<<dialog "Aldric">>
I know. Just   give me a second.
<</dialog>>

I didn't get a second. The first goblin appeared at the pit's edge, peering down with gleaming eyes. It grinned   goblins always grinned, it was the teeth   and raised its cleaver.

Mira's short sword took its head off. Single stroke, clean, the blade passing through the neck with barely a sound. The body stood there for a moment   headless, still grinning   then toppled into the pit between us, splashing rank water across my chest.

<<dialog "Mira">>
I need both hands. This is going to hurt.
<</dialog>>

<<dialog "Aldric">>
It already hurts.
<</dialog>>

<<dialog "Mira">>
It's going to hurt more.
<</dialog>>

<img src="img/scene/day_2/18.png" style="width: 100%; max-width: 768px; margin: 0 auto;" />

She sheathed the sword. Braced her feet against the pit wall. Grabbed the timber with both hands. She didn't pull this time   she pushed, using her legs as leverage, her arms rigid, her whole body a lever. The beam groaned. Creaked. Shifted sideways with a scraping sound I felt in my teeth.

The gap widened. Half an inch. An inch. Enough.

I wrenched my foot free.

The scream wasn't voluntary. It tore from my throat like something alive, and I buried it in my own forearm, biting down on leather and skin while my ankle throbbed with a deep grinding agony that pulsed in time with my heart. The splinter came out with the motion   mostly. I could feel a piece still in there, broken off inside the muscle, my calf swelling around it.

My ankle was a ruin. Expanding inside my boot, the leather tightening like a closing fist. Not broken   I thought   but torn. Twisted. Something ankles weren't meant to do.

Two more goblins dropped in. Mira killed the first with a knife   pulled from somewhere, the woman had weapons in every fold   a quick practiced stab through the soft tissue of the throat. Wet gargling. Collapse. She kicked the second into the far wall hard enough that its skull cracked against stone like a dropped melon.

I grabbed my longsword from the filthy water. Drove it through the stunned goblin's chest. The blade went in easy   goblin ribs were thin   and it spasmed once and went still.

<<dialog "Mira">>
Can you walk?
<</dialog>>

I tried weight on my right foot. The ankle folded. Not like a joint bending   like a building collapsing.

<<dialog "Aldric">>
No.
<</dialog>>

<<dialog "Mira">>
Can you crawl?
<</dialog>>

<<dialog "Aldric">>
Probably.
<</dialog>>

<<dialog "Mira">>
Then crawl.
<</dialog>>
