She was walking through the market. Slim and graceful, dark hair falling in waves past her shoulders, wearing fitted leather armor that hugged a body made of curves and angles that would stop traffic. She moved with purpose   not delicately, not tentatively, but with the direct, ground-eating stride of someone who knew how to fight. Just... differently. Hip-led. Balanced lower. A predator's walk translated into a different body.

